# Tests that measure the BUILD rather than behavior, and so cannot pass
# against an instrumented one. See ../scripts/branch-coverage.sh.
#
# Every entry needs its reason. A skipped test's arms simply go
# uncovered, so this file can only ever UNDERSTATE coverage.

# Asserts a 1 MiB allocation ceiling while scanning a 64 MiB value.
# gobco's per-condition counters in the byte lexer push it to ~3 MiB —
# still ~20x under the ~64 MiB a value-materializing tokenizer would
# cost, which is the failure mode the guard exists to catch. The
# property holds under instrumentation; only the slack does not.
^TestScanDuplicateKeysStreamsValues$
